@startuml crossexam-states
' What a claim's state can become in --mode crossexam.
' Traced against src/adversarial_friends/verdicts.py (state_for,
' should_discard, build_successor) and spec §7.1-§7.2.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam TitleFontSize 18

skinparam state {
  BorderColor #546E7A
  BackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  FontSize 13
  AttributeFontSize 12
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8E1
  BorderColor #F9A825
  FontSize 12
}

title Claim states in cross-examination

legend top right
  |<#C8E6C9>    | terminal, clears a gate |
  |<#FFCDD2>    | terminal, needs a human |
  |<#ECEFF1>    | another round could change it |
endlegend

state "contested" as C
state "settled-upheld" as SU #FFCDD2
state "settled-refuted" as SR #C8E6C9
state "superseded" as SUP #C8E6C9
state "deadlocked" as DL #FFCDD2
state "unproven" as UP
state "incomplete" as IN
state "discarded" as DIS #C8E6C9

[*] --> C : round 1 raised it

C --> SU : judges unanimously\n**upheld**
C --> SR : judges unanimously\n**refuted**
C --> SUP : judges unanimously\n**amended**
C --> C : rounds remain
C --> DL : judges disagree,\nno rounds left
C --> UP : below quorum
C --> IN : below quorum: a\nrequired judge is missing

UP --> C : a judge changed its mind
UP --> DIS : same verdict set\ntwo rounds running
IN --> C : the missing judge reported

SUP --> [*] : successor **c-NNNN@2**\nenters the next round as *contested*

note bottom of SU
  Not a pass. The judges agreed
  the defect is real, so a gate
  needs a Resolution, not silence.
end note

note bottom of DL
  Never resolved by majority.
  Both sides are quoted verbatim
  and the call is the reader's.
end note

note right of UP
  A dispositive verdict whose judge
  could not locate the evidence is
  downgraded to unproven first (§6.5),
  so nobody settles a claim by not
  having looked.
end note

@enduml
